-- title:
--   Hecke polynomials killing regular differentials kill J₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$ and assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeInputsAll N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeInputsAll.html#L8), i.e. that for every prime $\ell$ the package `HeckeInputsAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) N ℓ` holds: integrality of the two degeneracy maps `heckeAlphaBar` and `heckeBetaBar` from the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $N$ into that of level $N\ell$, the existence of principal divisors for the latter field, finiteness along `heckeAlphaBar`, together with the fundamental identity along `heckeBetaBar` and the norm formula along `heckeAlphaBar` (exactly the data under which `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ` is the correspondence-induced endomorphism of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ rather than $0$). Let $p$ be an element of the free $\mathbb Z$-algebra on the set of primes. Assume that for every $\omega$ in `regularDifferentialsBar N` — the submodule of $\Omega_{\overline{\mathbb Q}F_N/\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ consisting of those $\omega$ for which, at each place $v$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}F_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, one has $\omega = f \cdot v.\mathrm{dCoord}$ for some $f$ in the valuation subring of $v$ — the image of $p$ under the $\mathbb Z$-algebra map sending the indeterminate at $\ell$ to the opposite-ring element of the differential Hecke operator `heckeDiffBar N ℓ` (the correspondence attached to `heckeBetaBar`, `heckeAlphaBar`), read back in $\operatorname{End}(\Omega_{\overline{\mathbb Q}F_N/\overline{\mathbb Q}})$, annihilates $\omega$; because the lift is taken into the opposite ring, this is evaluation of $p$ with the order of products reversed. The conclusion is that the image of $p$ under the $\mathbb Z$-algebra map sending the indeterminate at $\ell$ to `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ` is the zero endomorphism of `JZero N` $= \mathrm{Pic}^0(\overline{\mathbb Q}F_N)$.
--
--   This is the faithfulness of the cotangent (analytic) representation of the Hecke algebra on the Jacobian $J_0(N)$: a noncommutative integral Hecke polynomial that annihilates $H^0(X_0(N)_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}, \Omega^1)$ annihilates $J_0(N)$ itself. It is used in [`ModularCurve.exists_injective_ringHom_adjoin_heckeOperatorBar_cuspForm`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_injective_ringHom_adjoin_heckeOperatorBar_cuspForm) to embed the ring generated by the Hecke operators on $J_0(N)$ into the Hecke algebra acting on weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_0(N)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_freeAlgebra_lift_heckeOperatorBar_eq_zero_of_lift_heckeDiffBar_eq_zero.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_HeckeModule
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_HeckeInputsAll
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_HeckeDifferential

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
